# MCSP Closed Round-Trip 0.43

Status: Constructive integrated qualification experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parents: 0.39, 0.40, 0.41, 0.42

## Objective

Compose the previously separated bounded mechanisms into one path:

    semantic pre-settlement
    -> MCSP assembly decision
    -> machine bytes
    -> machine execution
    -> MCSP disassembly
    -> structural tuple
    -> MCSP decompilation
    -> reconstructed semantic structure

The final reconstructed semantic structure SHALL preserve every material field admitted by this fixture.

## Original semantic structure

    width = 64
    source-preserved = 1
    destination-replaced = 1
    relation rows:
      00->0
      01->1
      10->1
      11->0

## Intermediate structural tuple

    relation-token = 1
    width = 64
    destination-register-token = 0
    source-register-token = 3
    operand-form = register/register

## Machine realization

Qualified target encoding:

    48 31 d8

The executable harness may append RET as a call boundary. RET is not part of the semantic target operation.

## Attacks

The integrated fixture SHALL reject:
- a mutated machine opcode;
- a reconstructed semantic relation containing 11->1;
- unsupported structural inputs.

The test SHALL not use mnemonic text as semantic authority.

## Qualification meaning

A PASS establishes bounded semantic preservation across the composed 0.39-0.42 path on the tested x86-64 fixture.

It does not establish:
- a general assembler;
- a general disassembler;
- a general decompiler;
- cross-ISA closed-round-trip preservation;
- self-description closure.

Kernel remains DETERMINATE CONDITION.
